# ER-Archipelago superrepo .gitignore
# The forks are SUBMODULES (tracked by gitlink, not by content here): the 6 4laric forks
# plus your Paramdex and yet-another-tab-control forks. Everything below is NOT committed.

# --- non-repo vendored / large dirs ---
# Contains the copyrighted game exe + vanilla param dumps. NEVER commit (licensing).
# BOTH forms: the trailing-slash rule matches a DIRECTORY only, but the sandbox clone uses a
# SYMLINK (AGENTS.md S5), which git then reports as an untracked FILE -- one `git add -A` from
# being committed to a public repo. Match it either way.
/elden_ring_artifacts/
/elden_ring_artifacts
# AP generation test output (zips, logs, per-run dirs) -- transient, keep it out.
/gen-test/*
# ...but the FILL-REGRESSION SUITE under it is SOURCE, not output, and hiding it was a mistake.
# run_fill_regression.ps1 -- which run_ci.ps1 runs as its FILL gate -- drives gen_sweep.ps1 over
# gen-test\fill-regression-yamls (one yaml per historically-recorded fill bug) and compares each
# config's pass-rate to a floor recorded in baseline.json. Those floors ARE the record of which fill
# bugs are fixed and how well they must keep passing. Untracked, they live on exactly one machine:
# a fresh clone makes run_fill_regression throw "suite folder not found", and `-UpdateBaseline` can
# lower a floor with nobody able to review the diff. Track the yamls and the baseline; keep the
# sweep OUTPUT ignored.
!/gen-test/fill-regression-yamls/
/gen-test/fill-regression-yamls/*
!/gen-test/fill-regression-yamls/*.yaml
!/gen-test/fill-regression-yamls/baseline.json
# Downloaded Nexus randomizer package.
/Elden Ring Randomizer-428-v0-11-4-1763103112 (2)/

# --- generated / build outputs ---
# packaged apworld (rebuilt by build.ps1) -- comment on its own line; inline # breaks the pattern
eldenring.apworld
eldenring_*.apworld
gensweep*
genfuzz*
genfuzz_ci_*.csv
genfuzz_ci_*.md
# bake output (slot/seed/location_flags)
apconfig.json
preflight_*.log
*.log
# 🛑 EXCEPT the sweep/kill correlator's fixtures (#713). They are hand-built CLIENT LOGS and are
# the acceptance for tools/check_sweep_kill_correlation.py -- ignored, they would vanish from the
# commit and the gate would go green on nothing. Named .log deliberately: the tool's whole job is
# parsing this grammar, and a fixture renamed to dodge an ignore rule stops being the real shape.
!greenfield/eldenring/tests/fixtures/*.log
# per-gen compact diagnostic (dlcdiag.py output; raw .log already ignored)
gendiag_*.txt

# --- backups / archives ---
*.bak
*.tar.gz

# --- python cache ---
__pycache__/
*.pyc

# --- OS / editor
# --- boss-attribution dry-run analysis outputs (regenerate via boss_attribution_dryrun.py / tune_complement.py) ---
boss-attribution-dryrun.csv
check-nearest-grace.csv
smithing_stone_distribution.csv

# --- tagged editor backups (the *.bak rule above misses *.bak_<tag>) ---
*.bak_*

# --- diag dumps (apworld gen / sphere-tier) ---
ER_DIAG.txt
ER_SPHERE_TIERS_*.txt

# --- Rust build output (rust-client-spike / fswap-er-client-pr crates) ---
target/


# --- AP run logs / probe temp (were committed before these rules existed) ---
ap_bake_*.log
ap_error_*.txt
ap-client-log.txt
_dg_tmp.py
.write_test_xyz

# --- large build / deploy outputs (regenerable) ---
# A trailing '#' does NOT start a comment in .gitignore -- only a '#' at the START of a line does.
# These three carried inline comments, so the patterns were literally "/build/   # ap_icon build
# output (~3 GB)" and matched NOTHING. All three were inert, including /applied_patches/, whose own
# comment says it holds regulation.bin. In a PUBLIC repo. Comments go on their own line.
# ap_icon build output (~3 GB)
/build/
# deployed mod runtime: eldenring_archipelago.dll, apconfig.json, ap-package (repainted textures)
/me3/
# applied-patch output incl. regulation.bin (game data)
/applied_patches/

# --- diag dumps / bake snapshots (regenerable) ---
ap_uncovered_flags_*.txt
apconfig_max.json
apconfig_snapshot*.json
lotmap.json
runtime.me3
# stray duplicate of the canonical table (source of truth = Archipelago/worlds/eldenring/)
/er_static_detection_table.json

# --- one-off patch scripts (transient; applied then discarded) ---
patch_*.py

# --- personal scratch yamls (shareable config = EldenRing-MASTER-template.yaml) ---
/EldenRing-Alaric.regionlock.yaml
/EldenRing-AlaricBase.yaml

# --- internal memory mirrors: do NOT commit to the public repo ---
/trust-alaric-cleared-layers.md
/er-ap-icon-override.md
/er-artifacts-tooling.md
/MEMORY.md

# --- retired baker-era deploy artifact: pure-runtime touches no game files ---
/deploy_manifest.txt

# --- seed-parking: keep metadata (.ps1/.txt/.yaml/.md), NEVER the deployed game blobs ---
# game-files/ = provisioned map/event/msg/script .dcx + regulation.bin (copyrighted, generated).
# save/ = ER0000.sl2 personal saves. mods/ = compiled archipelago.dll. ap-server/ = AP_*.zip output.
# _pre-restore-backup-*/ = full duplicate snapshot of all of the above.
seeds-archive/*/game-files/
seeds-archive/*/save/
seeds-archive/*/mods/
seeds-archive/*/ap-server/
seeds-archive/**/_pre-restore-backup-*/
# Save files are never source, anywhere in the tree.
*.sl2

# --- vendored / scratch dirs that must NOT be committed to the superrepo ---
# Vanilla game data dump (copyrighted; same rule as /elden_ring_artifacts/). NEVER commit.
/vanilla-game-snapshot/
# PR-prep scratch (duplicate source copies + draft bodies/plans).
/fswap-er-client-pr/
# Third-party Seamless Co-op mod config.
/seamless-coop/
# SoulsFormatsNEXT CI scratch (bui

# --- detection-table regen artifacts (regenerate via regenerate_detection_table.py; canonical = Archipelago/worlds/eldenring/) ---
er_static_detection_table_augmented_*.json
detection_table_added_*.txt
er_detection_table_missing_*.txt
# --- truncation backups + one-off slot_data verification baselines ---
*.truncbak
slot_data_baseline_*.json

# --- gen/CI diagnostic dumps + logs (regenerate on demand; never ship) ---
gendiag_*.txt
generate_*.log
generate_greenfield_*.log
genfuzz_ci_*.csv
genfuzz_ci_*.md
gensweep_*.csv
gensweep_*.md
preflight_*.log
elden_ring_artifacts/

# --- build outputs + local state: NEVER commit (2026-07-11 cleanup) ---
# Release packages belong in GitHub Releases, not git. 50 files / 79 MB of RETIRED v0.1
# artifacts were tracked here.
/dist/
# The client .dll is a BUILD OUTPUT (build.ps1 -Me3Deploy stages it). 7.8 MB, and a NEW blob
# entered history on every rebuild -- that alone is most of the 174 MB .git.
/me3/*.dll
# Local runtime state, not source. ap_save_*.json is a PLAYER SAVE, committed to a PUBLIC repo.
/me3/ap_save_*.json
/me3/apconfig.json

# Local Archipelago checkout (bootstrap-ap). NOT a submodule: it is a stock upstream clone,
# pinned by .ap-version. Nothing of ours lives in it -- the world is INSTALLED into it.
/Archipelago/
.ap-test/
dist/

# Dev-only region-correctness oracle (tools/dev/check_vs_matt.py) + its private thefifthmatt
# snapshot. NEVER committed: it references his copyrighted list as a differential oracle. Keeping
# it out of the tree keeps this repo clean-room. See tools/dev/README.md.
tools/dev/

# --- foreign randomizer location lists (PROVENANCE.md) ---
# Reading another project's list to cross-check is fine; committing it is not.
# tools/diff_foreign_list.py reads one from your own disk and writes nothing back.
# tools/check_integrity.py refuses to commit a file carrying the key grammar; this is
# the belt to that braces, so a list parked in the tree never even shows up as untracked.
/foreign/
itemslots.yaml
items.txt
locationIdsToKeys*.json
*.foreign-list

# tools/fill_regression.py writes its logs + results.json into a timestamped dir in the REPO ROOT
# (fillreg_YYYYMMDD-HHMMSS/). Running the gate locally before pushing is the point -- see
# CONTRIBUTING -- so this lands in a working tree routinely, and `git add -A` swept 1224 lines of
# results.json into a commit once. Ignore the artifact, not the habit.
fillreg_*/

# tools/gen_enemy_drop_entities.py (#1000) writes its Rust rows into the CWD by default. It is a
# local-only tool run from the repo root, so the artifact lands in a working tree routinely and is
# one `git add -A` from being committed. Ignore the artifact, not the habit (see fillreg_* above).
enemy_drop_entities.rows

# --- region second-opinion audit: raw wiki API responses (tools/audit_region_second_opinion.py).
# The tool defaults its cache OUTSIDE the tree; this catches an in-tree --cache. Wiki prose must
# never be committed -- only our verdicts, our region names and page titles as citations.
.er-region-audit-cache/
